  {
   "name": "The Sagrada Família",
   "aka": [
    "Basílica de la Sagrada Família",
    "Temple Expiatori de la Sagrada Família"
   ],
   "at": [
    41.403621,
    2.17403
   ],
   "model": "sagrada",
   "face": 134.7,
   "info": "Gaudí's basilica, begun in 1882 and his work from 1883 until he died in 1926; still building. In 2026, the centenary of his death, the Tower of Jesus Christ was finished at 172.5 m with its cross of glass and white ceramic: the tallest church tower in the world, a metre short of Montjuïc, as Gaudí wanted. Round it the four Evangelists' towers (135 m) with their bull, lion, eagle and angel, and the Virgin Mary's (138 m) with its star; eight of the twelve Apostles' spires stand over the Nativity and Passion fronts. The Glory front, the main one, is under the cranes.",
   "clearArea": {
